# ── Internal, not published ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/architecture/ is public — it is the technical documentation, and it is
# the reason a stranger can tell this was built by people who understand it.
# The rest is the business of running the project, not of using the code:
# strategy, pricing, market sizing, competitor analysis, launch gates, and our
# own agent working agreements. Publishing those hands a stranger the pricing
# model and the roadmap. They stay on disk and stay versioned locally; they are
# simply not in this repository.
/docs/product/
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/CONTRIBUTING.md
/CLAUDE.md
/phase1.md

# Tracking is not the same as publishing, and the two used to be conflated —
# the failure was silent in both directions. A new doc under docs/product/ used
# to be a no-op to `git add`, so a launch-gating document could go unwritten
# from the team's point of view. The fix is scoping, not blanket ignoring: one
# tree ships, the other does not.

# The old note this replaced, kept because the history matters: /docs/ and
# /CLAUDE.md were ignored here while 27 files under docs/ were
# already tracked (force-added). That made the lines inert for existing
# files and actively harmful for new ones: every new doc was local-only
# unless you remembered `git add -f`, including release-plan.md and
# cws-submission.md, which gate the Chrome Web Store submission. Both are
# now tracked and the ignore rules are gone.

# Local agent config — absolute paths and per-machine permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local scratch previews
.preview/

# Visual brainstorming companion
.superpowers/
